  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to the Development of Area C through the EU in Palestine (2016-2020)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x201c;Local communities are better able to sustain their livelihoods in Area C through improved access to basic services and infrastructure&#x201d;.

1.	Output 1: Baseline (2017): 1,200  Result (2020): 2,793  
Provision of legal information and counselling, training and technical assistance to vulnerable Palestinian households and communities, Palestinian Authority, Local Government Units, Ministerial Directorates and aid agencies on the domestic and internal law implications of building, or facing seizure of equipment specific to the nature of projects they are engaged in.

2.	Output 2 &#x2013; Baseline (2017): 144   Result (2020): 296  
Provision of legal representation to vulnerable Palestinian households and communities, LGUs and ministerial directorates in cases related to demolition, stop work and eviction orders, settler violence and takeover of land, military seizure of land or equipment, freedom of movement restrictions including the seam zone, road blocks and closed military areas.

3.	Output 3: Baseline (2017): 2   Result (2020): 6
Principled legal interventions on behalf of communities/LGUs/Directorates will be undertaken to challenge unjust policies, laws and practices.</narrative>
  </description>
